  "narration": "Elephants can send messages through the ground. Their deep rumbles do not only travel through the air. Part of the vibration couples into the soil and moves outward as a seismic signal. Another elephant can detect those vibrations through sensitive structures in its feet and trunk. Researchers have observed animals freeze, lean forward, and shift weight toward their front feet while listening. These low-frequency signals may help herds coordinate, recognize warnings, and stay connected over long distances. To an elephant, the ground is not silent. It is another communication channel.",
